{
  "id": "T18_57_a_normalization_is_validated_on_write_and_never_withdrawn",
  "family": "T18",
  "rules": [
    "10.2.4",
    "10.2.6",
    "10.2.7",
    "7.3.8",
    "8.4.1",
    "2.4.4",
    "6.7.9",
    "8.3.1",
    "10.4.1"
  ],
  "description": "A normalization must have exactly one target that is an Item reference (two Items, or an Assertion reference, fail 10.2.6) and must carry @interpretation, null or {name, version} (missing, a string, or an object without a version fails 10.2.4). Its @effective may be later than its occurrence time but not earlier (10.2.7). A well-formed normalization with a later @effective is accepted and applies from that instant. A reconciliation with @outcome reinterpret, and @interpretation on a review, fail 10.2.4. A withdrawal of the normalization fails 10.2.6. A correction that replaces it with another interpretation is accepted, and reads use the corrected normalization.",
  "note": "7.3.8: a normalization is an act whose values carry `@action: \"reinterpret\"`; \"exactly one target in `@targets`, an Item reference naming a scope Item (2.1.5); and `@interpretation`, naming the interpretation as `{ \"name\", \"version\" }`, or `null` for literal comparison\". \"It is never withdrawn (6.7.9) ... a misrecorded one is corrected (8.3).\" README section 6, item 8: \"a `@targets` that is a list of references but not exactly one Item reference is `10.2.6`; an `@interpretation` that is missing, or that is neither `null` nor `{\\\"name\\\": <string>, \\\"version\\\": <string>}`, is `10.2.4`. A reconciliation with `\\\"@outcome\\\": \\\"reinterpret\\\"` is an undefined value of a defined member and fails `10.2.4` (10.4.1). `@effective` is allowed on a normalization and on an `adopt_policy` (8.4.1).\"",
